  "in_scope": [
    "Prove the four requirements per reachable surface: it compiles from a canonical IOI catalog; its taxonomy, labels, and examples are IOI-owned; it contains no externally derived branding, assets, links, product vocabulary, or implementation fallback; and anything not operationally bound is omitted or marked unavailable in the product's own honest-state vocabulary rather than presented as working.",
    "Take the retained census artifact internal-docs/prompts/architecture-relative-comparison/runs/2026-07-28-leg0-v2-external-reference-residue-census.md as the defect baseline: 146 actionable rows across the served estate, with exactly one surface family carrying no family-specific residue.",
    "Account for the two structural multipliers the baseline records, because a naive row count understates the fix surface. First, every shell row exists twice on disk — the served bundle is duplicated, and the copy that is NOT the conventional one is the default served tree when the serving environment variable is unset, so a repair applied to one tree leaves the default path unrepaired. Second, one shared chrome line renders on all fourteen registry surfaces, so a single edit is either an estate-wide repair or an estate-wide finding.",
    "Detect residue that no text search can find. The baseline records external product names, external case-study copy, a third-party logo grid, and a synthetic clinical record baked into raster assets that are embedded as data URIs and decoded only at render; the check must read what a surface actually presents, including accessible names, image content, and tab titles, not only its source strings.",
    "Cover the live application launcher compiled from an externally derived catalog, and the rendered links that route a user out of first-party copy into externally derived material; the launcher's own availability obligation is owned separately by p2-launcher-catalog-availability-check and is joined, not duplicated, here.",
    "State and verify the rule source-neutrally: prohibited residue is detected by what the surface presents and where it was compiled from, never by matching a frozen list of external names."
  ],
  "out_of_scope": [
    "Unreachable internal or reference material — research corpora, capture archives, reharvest tooling, and verifier fixtures that assert absence rather than leak it. The baseline reports these separately and they are non-blocking.",
    "Properly licensed and attributed third-party dependencies, including an attributed open-source icon set carried with its notice in place. External origin is not a finding; stripping a required attribution would be one.",
    "Application operational depth: whether a surface's faculties are implemented is a different obligation than whether it tells the truth about what it is and what is bound.",
    "Visual parity with any external reference, in either direction. Parity is never evidence that a surface is bound, and divergence from an external reference is never a finding."
  ],
